\lispPackageChapter{candlesticks/instruments}

An instrument is one tradable thing: a stock, bond, cryptocurrency,
commodity, currency, index, or anything else that exists in a fungible
traded market.  Identity is the \textsc{Uuid}.  Short market
abbreviations are \texttt{tickers}, because the same abbreviation can
mean different instruments at different sources.

\section{Types}

\lispTypeSubsection{instrument}

A CLOS class with slots \texttt{id}, \texttt{name},
\lispId{instrument-type-id}, and \lispId{instrument-type}.  The accessors
have the obvious names.  \texttt{instrumentp} is true of instances.
\texttt{name} is a human label such as \texttt{"Bitcoin"} and is not
unique.

\section{Functions}

\lispFunctionSubsection{make-instrument}

Create a new instrument and return it.  Identity is the \textsc{Uuid};
attach market abbreviations with \texttt{make-ticker} or
\lispId{ensure-instrument-for-ticker}.

\lispSyntax

\lispCall{\texttt{(make-instrument \&key \lispVar{name} \lispVar{instrument-type})}}

\lispFunctionSubsection{fill-instrument}

Fill in any missing name or type on an existing instrument, without
overwriting values that are already set.

\lispFunctionSubsection{instrument-by-id}

The instrument with the given \textsc{Uuid}, or \texttt{nil}.

\lispFunctionSubsection{all-instruments}

Every instrument, alphabetically by name.
